We have a larger problem that needs to get addressed.  It belongs to the issue of General Tour description if/when the exhibition was found  on the museum\'92s site; here at https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound#paragraph--185861.  We described the tour via the stops we obtained; this is our General tour description: \'93You are about to explore the Picasso, Miro, Dali: Unbound exhibition at MFA in Boston. Encounter three distinctive works within this collection: Le L\'e9zard aux plumes d\'92or (The Lizard with Golden Feathers), Moses and Monotheism, and Au Soleil du Plafond. Witness how these artists draw inspiration from diverse sources, shaping their creations to reflect a fascinating fusion of the world around them, their inner beliefs, and their boundless creativity. At Le L\'e9zard aux plumes d\'92or, prepare to challenge reality and imagination through the masterpiece on display. Then, at Moses and Monotheism, experience the solemnity and timelessness enhanced by the monochromatic color palette. Your first stop is Le L\'e9zard aux plumes d\'92or (The Lizard with Golden Feathers)\'94  And that is not bad: all parts are good: introduction, works, reference to the works and finally naming the first stop.  The problem is that we said nothing about the exhibit narration: why someone put the collection together, what entity it is showing.  Google did a much better job when I asked it, \'91
\f1 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What is "Picasso, Mir\'f3, Dal\'ed: Unbound" MFA Exhibition all about?
\f0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \'92  This is the answer:\
\'97\'97\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The exhibition 
\f2\b \'93Picasso, Mir\'f3, Dal\'ed: Unbound\'94
\f0\b0  at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Museum of Fine Arts, Boston}} is \cb4 \strokec2 dedicated to the 
\f2\b \cb4 \strokec2 revolutionary world of 
\f3\i livres d\'92artiste
\f2\i0  (artist's books)
\f0\b0 \cb1 \strokec2 . Running from 
\f2\b August 1, 2026, to January 24, 2027
\f0\b0 , the show explores how 20th-century avant-garde Spanish masters upended traditional publishing by turning books into a dynamic space for fine art. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bonart.cat/en/n/47016/picasso-miro-and-dali-reinvent-the-book-as-a-work-of-art-at-the-mfa-in-boston"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://exploreboston.com/events/picasso-miro-dali-unbound-opens-at-the-mfa/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}]\
Rather than treating books as mere containers for text, these artists merged imagery, typography, paper selection, and binding into a singular visual discourse. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.timeout.com/boston/things-to-do/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bonart.cat/en/n/47016/picasso-miro-and-dali-reinvent-the-book-as-a-work-of-art-at-the-mfa-in-boston"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}]\
