\cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The second problem is that we are treating the works of Spanish painters completely outside of the exhibit intend: exhibit wanted to show 
\fs32 \outl0\strokewidth0 how 20th-century avant-garde Spanish masters upended traditional publishing by turning books into a dynamic space for fine art. Rather than treating books as mere containers for text, these artists merged imagery, typography, paper selection, and binding into a singular visual discourse. But we are pointing listeners to \'93The meticulous attention to detail in rendering the reptile's intricate plumage contrasts with the wild, untamed nature of the surrounding foliage, creating a tension between the familiar and the fantastical. This masterpiece challenges the boundaries between reality and imagination.\'94 completely forgetting about the main point: these is a new art: illustrated books.\
\
The third problem is that there are no stories.  Listeners are not intrigued by the artists, diners, curators, MFA, nothing.  This is Storied release, and no stories demonstrate our failure.\
\
All three problems must be fixed.  We are paying attention to the credibility of sources; and this is good, but without stories, the tour does not worth much, and people will not pay for it.
